  "body": {
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every \\(2\\leq k\\leq m\\) and \\(r\\geq1\\),\n\\[\n mr\\leq s_\\star(m,r,k)\\leq 2mr-m.\n\\]\nConsequently \\(s_\\star(m,r,k)=\\Theta(mr)\\) uniformly in \\(k\\).  The upper bound simultaneously controls the two separately minimized endpoint supports \\(s_L(o,e)\\) and \\(s_U(o,e)\\) for every \\((o,e)\\in\\mathcal C_{m,r,k}\\).  The lower bound is witnessed by the compatible family \\(o_{is}=1/(mr)\\), \\(e_{js}=1/r\\), for which both endpoint support minima are at least \\(mr\\).  Hence the quadratic \\(k^2\\) term in \\(N_\\star\\) is not intrinsic to exact endpoint witnesses.",
    "justification": "A finite-rank endpoint-face compression and a forced-positive-cell witness give matching linear order in the number of observational cells.",
    "gap": "This closes the former support-frontier question and separates intrinsic support from the quadratic overhead of the explicit flow realization.",
    "consumer": "An audit standard may require only order \\(mr\\) response atoms for exact endpoint existence, although the direct constructive certificate retains its larger explicit bound.",
    "id": "thm:resolve-8a9c8a8bd2d8784d542c",
    "depends_on": [
      "def:support-compression-handle",
      "thm:sharp-interval",
      "thm:algorithmic-certificates",
      "thm:optimal-support-frontier-order"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "This is exactly the claim of thm:optimal-support-frontier-order; apply thm:optimal-support-frontier-order.",
